From 45f7f41aaa1d7f591453a8067cdb8b26c647d3c5 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: forge-shepherd <noreply@anthropic.com>
Date: Thu, 16 Jul 2026 13:29:16 +0530
Subject: [PATCH] feat(monitor): land an actionable pr-verdict:* label on
 pr-monitor (b5c154cd)
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

The pr-monitor workflow already auto-runs on every PR and keeps one sticky
comment current, but it posts PROSE only — no cheap machine-readable signal.
Agents/humans still had to parse the comment or poll gh. This adds the missing
actionable layer to the EXISTING subsystem (no new workflow):

- lib/pr-verdict.js: computeVerdict over the SAME bundle the monitor gathers.
  Vocabulary + priority mirror the canonical `forge shepherd --pull --json`
  ladder (unknown > conflict > behind > check-failed > threads-open > pending >
  mergeable) so the label never disagrees with --pull. Fail-closed.
- pr-monitor.yml: after the sticky upsert, reconcile EXACTLY ONE `pr-verdict:*`
  label (add chosen, strip stale) — the cheap agent read (gh pr view --json
  labels). scripts/pr-verdict-label.js is the thin emit glue.
- render-sticky.js: lead the sticky with the one-line verdict headline and
  reconcile the "never a verdict" wording — it now LABELS state but still never
  merges and never resolves threads.

Surface only, agent-agnostic: labels state, never merges, never resolves threads.
Verified live: computeVerdict over PR #403's bundle yields pr-verdict:behind,
matching `forge shepherd 403 --pull --json` (verdict BEHIND).

Refs: b5c154cd (verdict label), epic c2d398e5. Read-CLI stays filed as e2420489.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 4.8 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>
